{
  "Name": "Kimai v0.9.2 'db_restore.php' SQL Injection",
  "Description": "This module exploits a SQL injection vulnerability in Kimai version 0.9.2.x. The 'db_restore.php' file allows unauthenticated users to execute arbitrary SQL queries. This module writes a PHP payload to disk if the following conditions are met: The PHP configuration must have 'display_errors' enabled, Kimai must be configured to use a MySQL database running on localhost; and the MySQL user must have write permission to the Kimai 'temporary' directory.",
